{
 "schema": "148ai.page_types/1",
 "_about": "Warehouse 123 (released by the owner 2026-11-27, inbox/004): the page types of a website. Today the engine has two output families (website, web_app); a website is one of eight page types, and each type is a SKELETON: which sections, in what order, which of them the type cannot do without, the image-to-text ratio it aims at, and the threshold table its gates judge it by. The model fills a skeleton; it does not copy a page. Every entry is source 'seed': written by hand from the section library (omni_prod/section_library, the keys of its ORDER), not extracted from a corpus. A corpus run (warehouse 120: five to eight real pages of the type) replaces an entry and sets source 'corpus' with 'corpus_pages'; check() refuses a 'corpus' entry without them. The detector reads 'cues': a cue is a word the customer wrote, with the weight of how strongly it names the type (3 names it, 2 leans, 1 hints; weak cues are capped). The stable key is the type's id (the key of 'types'): `page_type`. Fields that belong to item 122 (required FIELDS per type) are not here. 'sections' are section_library keys only; a section a type needs that the library does not have is named in 'not_in_library' and never faked. Thresholds: [min, max], measured on the rendered page (page_types.measure).",
